          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In a formal language such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            or
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            of the terms of the language.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %strong judgmental equality
            = succeed "," do
              %strong propositional equality
            = succeed "." do
              %strong typal equality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicate+logic+over+type+theory"} predicate logic over type theory
          %p
            %strong> Note
            \: In this article, we use the term
            %em propositional equality
            in the sense of equality as a proposition and proposition as different from types. In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+subsingletons"} propositions as subsingletons
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions+as+types"} propositions as types
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality#InDependentTypeTheory"} propositional equality § In dependent type theory
          %h3#judgmental_equality Judgmental equality
          %p
            The first notion of equality is
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgment"} judgment
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash (t:A)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi t
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash (t = t'): A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
          %p
            However, not all type theories have judgmental equality; most
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theories"} first-order theories
            use propositional equality in place of judgmental equality, and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theories"} objective type theories
            use typal equality in place of judgmental equality.
          %h3#propositional_equality Propositional equality
          %p
            In any two-layer type theory with a layer of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            and a layer of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first order logic
            over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            or a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has a binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            according to which two elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            are related if and only if they are equal; in this case we write
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %msub
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x =_A y
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+equality"} propositional equality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi x
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A, y:A \vdash x =_A y \; \mathrm{prop}} \quad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma, x:A \vdash x =_A x \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p Then we have the elimination rules for propositional equality:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A, y:A, x =_A y \; \mathrm{true} \vdash P(x, y) \; \mathrm{prop} \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash P(x, x) \; \mathrm{true}}{\Gamma, x:A, y:A, x =_A y \; \mathrm{true} \vdash P(x, y) \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p
            Propositional equality satisfies the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+substitution"} principle of substitution
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+of+indiscernibles"} identity of indiscernibles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⇔
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma, x:A \vdash P(x) \; \mathrm{prop}}{\Gamma, x:A, y:A \vdash (x =_A y) \implies (P(x) \iff P(y)) \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p In addition, one could have propositional equality between the types themselves, with formation and introduction rules
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} prop
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash B \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash A = B \; \mathrm{prop}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash A = A \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p
            Notable examples of propositional equality include the equality in all flavors of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set+theory"} set theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
          %p
            The presence of propositional equality is part of the axiomatization of first-order theories, although this is usually swept under the rug by including propositional equality by default in all first-order theories. (It has to be made more explicit in a structural set theory such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SEAR"} SEAR
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            which has to be put onto a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preset"} preset
          %h3#typal_equality Typal equality
          %p
            However, not all type theories are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+order+logic"} first order logic
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/typal+equality"} typal equality
            = succeed "," do
              %strong equality type
            = succeed "," do
              %strong identity type
            = succeed "," do
              %strong path type
            = succeed "," do
              %strong identification type
            = succeed "," do
              %strong equalities
            = succeed "," do
              %strong identities
            = succeed "," do
              %strong identifications
            = succeed "." do
              %strong paths
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+observational+type+theory"} higher observational type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+path+type"} cubical path type
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
          %p
            Type theories with only typal equality are called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theories"} objective type theories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intensional+type+theories"} intensional type theories
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensional+type+theories"} extensional type theories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi b
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo ≡
                        %mi A
                      %mi b
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash p:a =_A b}{\Gamma \vdash a \equiv b:A} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash p:a =_A b}{\Gamma \vdash a \equiv_A b \; \mathrm{true}}
          %p
            Intensional type theories are then type theories with typal equality and one of either judgmental or propositional equality without an equality reflection rule. Note that this notion of extensionality is different from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+extensionality"} function extensionality
          %h3#comparison_of_equalities Comparison of equalities
          %p This table gives the six different notions of equality found in type theory.
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th Judgment
                %th of types
                %th of terms
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Judgmental equality
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash A = B \; \mathrm{type}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi a
                        %mo =
                        %mi b
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash a = b:A
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Propositional equality
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi B
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash A = B \; \mathrm{true}
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi a
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %mi b
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash a =_A b \; \mathrm{true}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Typal equality
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi P
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                        %mo ≡
                        %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash P:A \equiv B
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo ⊢
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi a
                        %msub
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma \vdash p:a =_A b
          %h2#structural_rules_of_equalities Structural rules of equalities
          %h3#reflexivity Reflexivity
          %p The reflexivity of equality is given by the following judgmental, propositional, and typal rules respectively:
          %ul
            %li Reflexivity of judgmental equality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash A = A \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi a
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A}{\Gamma \vdash a = a:A}
          %ul
            %li
              %p Reflexivity of propositional equality
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash A = A \; \mathrm{true}}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mo =
                            %mi A
                          %mi a
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} true
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A}{\Gamma \vdash a =_A a \; \mathrm{true}}
            %li
              %p
                Reflexitivity of typal equality (i.e.
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+function"} identity function
                and identity
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path"} path
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %msub
                            %mi id
                            %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash id_{A}:A \simeq A}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %msub
                            %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} refl
                            %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi a
                          %msub
                            %mo =
                            %mi A
                          %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash a:A}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{refl}_{A}(a):a =_A a}
          %h3#symmetry Symmetry
          %p The symmetry of equality is given by the following judgmental, propositional, and typal rules respectively:
          %ul
            %li
              %p Symmetry of judgmental equality
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mo =
                          %mi B
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi B
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A = B \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash B = A \; \mathrm{type}}
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi A
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                          %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi a
                          %mo =
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi Γ
                          %mo ⊢
                          %mi b
                          %mo =
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
