          %h2#usages_of_equality Usages of equality
          %h3#in_definitions_of_types_and_terms In definitions of types and terms
          %p
            The three different notions of equality above could be used in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitions"} definitions
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terms"} terms
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+assignment+operator"} single assignment operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≔
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coloneqq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theories"} objective type theories
          %h3#in_conversion_rules_and_inductive_definitions In conversion rules and inductive definitions
          %p
            The three different notions of equality above could also be used in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conversion+rules"} conversion rules
            for the various type formers, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/beta+conversion"} beta conversion
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eta+conversion"} eta conversion
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conversional+equality"} conversional equality
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %strong computational equality
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+definitions"} inductive definitions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin-L%C3%B6f+type+theory"} Martin-Löf type theory
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theories"} objective type theories
          %h2#metaequalities Meta-equalities
          %p
            There are also equalities in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            which are not internal to the type theory itself, but rather equalities in the metatheory. These include
            %strong syntactic equality
            of expressions, as well as
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/alpha-equivalence"} alpha-equivalence
            and
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/definitional+equality"} definitional equality
            of syntactical expressions. When using
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Bruijn+indices"} de Bruijn indices
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+variables"} bound variables
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MLTT"} MLTT
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cubical+type+theory"} cubical type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ETCS"} ETCS
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/judgmental+equality"} judgmental equality
            like
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objective+type+theories"} objective type theories
