          %h2#references References
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georg+Hegel"}> Georg Hegel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Science+of+Logic"} Science of Logic
          %p
            equality is the subject of volume 1, book 2 “Die Lehre vom Wesen” (The doctrine of essence). As discussed at
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Science+of+Logic"} Science of Logic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+types"} identity types
          %p
            Texts on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            typically deal with the subtleties of the notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %em equality
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Per+Martin-L%C3%B6f"}> Per Martin-Löf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Intuitionistic type theory
          %p Besides
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kurt+G%C3%B6del"}> Kurt Gödel
              ,
              = succeed "." do
                %em Über eine bisher noch nicht benützte Erweiterung des finiten Standpunktes
          %p which might be the first paper to mention intensional equality (and the fact that it should be decidable), there is
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolaas+de+Bruijn"}> Nicolaas de Bruijn
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Automath"} Automath
          %p where de Bruijn makes a distinction between definitional equality and “book” equality.
          %ul
            %li#Buzzard24
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Buzzard"}> Kevin Buzzard
              ,
              %em Grothendieck’s use of equality
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.10387"}> arXiv:2405.10387
              )
